#: bookmarks/templates/settings/general.html:469
msgid ""
"1. Rules affect domain filtering logic, reflected in the sidebar \"Domains\" "
"module and favicon-based domain filtering.<br> 2. Each line configures one "
"rule. There are two types of rules:<br> (1) Subdomain normalization: e.g., "
"<code>a.com</code> normalizes <code>1.a.com</code> and <code>2.a.com</code> "
"under <code>a.com</code><br> (2) Cross-domain mapping: e.g., <code>b.com -> "
"a.com</code> normalizes <code>1.b.com</code> and <code>2.b.com</code> under "
"<code>a.com</code><br> 3. After configuring a subdomain normalization rule "
"like <code>a.com</code>, adding a subdomain like <code>3.a.com</code> keeps "
"<code>3.a.com</code> unnormalized:<br> (1) In the sidebar \"Domains\" "
"module, <code>a.com</code> expands to show <code>3.a.com</code> "
"separately<br> (2) Clicking the favicon of <code>3.a.com</code> bookmarks "
"will not force filtering by <code>a.com</code><br> 4. After configuring a "
"cross-domain mapping rule like <code>b.com -> a.com</code>, adding a rule "
"like <code>b.com</code> keeps <code>b.com</code> unnormalized:<br> (1) In "
"the sidebar \"Domains\" module, <code>a.com</code> expands to show "
"<code>b.com</code> separately<br> (2) Clicking the favicon of <code>b.com</"
"code> bookmarks will not force filtering by <code>a.com</code>"
msgstr ""

